  "grade": "artifacts:control-open-timeout",
  "description": "open_shell's open_timeout (from proto_version 0.6): how long the worker waits for the target to open the shell, integer milliseconds, 1 to 2^53-1 (common duration_ms). Optional: an open_shell without it is valid, and absent means no bound — what an older core sends. The value is the config.yaml knob worker.open_timeout, or the target's own options.open_timeout, never a schema default (decision 5.36). A 0, a duration string or a value past 2^53-1 is refused. control-open-timeout grades that a core sends the field to every peer at 0.6 or later and to no older one; control-sequence validates each captured open_shell against this shape.",
  "corpus": [
    "immortality §6.4",
    "decision 5.36",
    "lang-arch §7.3",
    "plan.md §3 C3"
  ],
  "case": {
